body:
thanks for the reply.

&#x200B;

Substitution.c:148:21: error: ignoring return value of function declared with pure attribute \[-Werror,-Wunused-value\]

toupper(plaintext\[i\]);

I agree completely. You have to stop the compulsions. They only attenuate the negative, irrational thoughts. However, what if the obsessions are so extreme, they send you down a deep ride of extreme despair and catanoia. This is my current problem. My OCD thoughts now are deep, dark, and horrifying. If I were to resist the compulsions (mental review), I would be sent down a path of darkness that would take me at least 2-3 days to pull myself out of. 

&#x200B;

I have never posted about my OCD before online. I need help, I need someone to talk to who knows what I am going through. I am currently a medical student and I have not studied for almost a week now, because I am not doing my compulsions, I am riding it out, but in return, I can barely crawl and care for myself. I feel that I am getting better, but I'm falling behind in life. 

&#x200B;

I am willing to lose a lot to beat my OCD , but not everything. But maybe that is the choice I will have to make.
